From 680f75284d592c86a4a1b3ae08161f06aaa93d56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:59:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] softisp: Add lens shading correction

Add an Lsc algorithm to the simple IPA. It reads 17x13 R/G/B gain meshes
per colour temperature from the tuning file, interpolates them for the
AWB temperature and passes the result to the debayer as an RGBA8 mesh
(gain = 1 + value / 255 * range), re-encoded only on a temperature change
of 100K or more.

The GPU debayer uploads the mesh to texture unit 2 when its revision
changes and both Bayer shaders multiply each pixel by the linearly
filtered gain right after black level subtraction. Without Lsc tuning
lsc_range stays 0 and the shaders skip it. The CPU debayer ignores it.
